    apply: "Pray over your preparation and commit to complete the exam honestly. After the exam, write down one action from the course that you will keep for the next year. Thank those who have taught you, and ask God to keep the lessons alive in your habits.",
    activity: "The class sits the final examination under the teacher's supervision. Where the examination is held on another date, use this session for a final review and to answer questions. End with a prayer of thanks for the course and for each learner.",
    takeHome: "Review the revision map and memory verses. Reflect on one change you have made. Memorise Proverbs 17:17 and Romans 15:7.",
    prayer: "Ask for peace and clear thinking in the exam. Thank God for the course and for teachers. Pray that our learning would become lasting, godly relationships.",
    teacher: "Explain the format, timing and pass mark. Ensure a calm and fair environment, with support for learners who need special arrangements. Do not give answers during the exam. Afterward, release results according to church policy and encourage those who need to retake.",
    assess: "This unit is the final examination week. The final examination covers Lessons 1 to 24 and is built from the approved question bank following the curriculum blueprint.",
    mcq1: ["Which verse tells us that iron sharpens iron?", ["Proverbs 27:17", "Genesis 1:1", "Psalm 23", "John 3:16"], 0, "Proverbs 27:17."],
